# boot — top-level dinit target for the ReForge service chain.
#
# STATUS: staged. dinit is NOT PID 1 yet — today the chroot still boots via the
# sequential /mod/start.sh S-loop (see reforge-boot §7 in docs/boot.md). These
# service descriptions mirror that S-loop so that when dinit takes over as the
# switch_root PID 1 it supervises the same services with dependency ordering and
# restart-on-failure. Until then they are inert config.
#
# Dependency order falls out of the per-service depends-on/waits-for:
#   cloudblock, zram            (one-shots, no deps — run early, in parallel)
#   eboard -> klipper           (MCU handshake before klippy)
#   klipper -> moonraker        (moonraker waits for klippy's UDS)
#   moonraker -> httpd          (Mainsail served after the API is up)
#   {klipper,moonraker,httpd} -> ok   (LKG promote once everything is up)
#
# camera and guppyscreen are defined but intentionally NOT pulled in here: they
# are conditional (camera = /dev/video0 present; guppyscreen = SCREEN_MODE=GUPPY
# + /dev/fb0). A later SCREEN_MODE/camera selector starts them on demand.

type = internal
depends-on = cloudblock
depends-on = zram
depends-on = eboard
depends-on = klipper
depends-on = moonraker
depends-on = httpd
depends-on = ok
